        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Protected Audience APIs: Chrome 157 removes most but not all]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/31120</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/31120"/>
        <updated>2026-11-12T19:06:57.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64103?u=428d3c27c9cd7efc648e17dfe5a4321c3f8e44d2&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>
<p dir="auto">Chrome 157 removes most but not all of the Protected Audience API surface.</p>

<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>
<p dir="auto">This Chromium change removes the various <code class="notranslate">navigator</code> properties: <a href="https://chromiumdash.appspot.com/commit/7270d1697cac1d56b7f2cea82346076db5d43743" rel="nofollow">https://chromiumdash.appspot.com/commit/7270d1697cac1d56b7f2cea82346076db5d43743</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">Some APIs remain, mainly the <code class="notranslate">ProtectedAudience</code> interface itself. I can't confirm its removal just yet (it seems to be in either 159 or 160 but I get inconsistent testing results right now). <a href="https://chromiumdash.appspot.com/commit/2ae93f9b43b9bb8d54e382a9257ef950feaa308c" rel="nofollow">This Chromium change</a> says 159, but it's not removed in Browser Stack's Chrome 159, but it is removed in my local Canary 160. It might be that Browser Stack has an older build, so I decided to let this be inconclusive for now.</p>


<h4 dir="auto">Related issues</h4>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://chromiumdash.appspot.com/commit/7270d1697cac1d56b7f2cea82346076db5d43743" rel="nofollow">https://chromiumdash.appspot.com/commit/7270d1697cac1d56b7f2cea82346076db5d43743</a></li>
<li><a href="https://issues.chromium.org/issues/460501344" rel="nofollow">https://issues.chromium.org/issues/460501344</a></li>
</ul>

]]></content>
